# pdn_cfg_grx930.tcl -- the template's pdn_cfg.tcl without its SRAM stripe grid,
# for the grx930 chip-top run.
#
# Why this file exists: the template's pdn_cfg.tcl ends by sourcing
# pdn_5v_sram.tcl (or pdn_3v3_sram.tcl when SRAM_DEFINE says so), and those
# scripts call add_pdn_stripe / add_pdn_connect with -instances
# i_chip_core.sram_0 and i_chip_core.sram_1, the two foundry SRAM macros the
# template's demo chip_core.sv instantiates. Our chip_core_grx930.sv replaces
# that module and has no SRAM macro -- grx930's memory is behavioural RTL inside
# grx930_test_chip, inferred by synthesis -- so the grid would stripe around
# instances that do not exist. Same class of mismatch as the macro declaration
# that stopped run ws_v1 at step 11 (OpenROAD.CheckMacroInstances).
#
# Everything else is the template's file byte for byte: the pad-ring stitches,
# the core ring and the macro grid, which are what this design does need. If the
# generic part of the template's pdn_cfg.tcl changes, re-copy it rather than
# editing this by hand.

